oblastomas\" as Specific Disease around 559-580. I'm cross-checking these spans against the actual substrings to make sure the lengths and positions line up correctly before finalizing the annotation list.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"annotations\":[{\"start\":68,\"end\":102,\"text\":\"brain, breast, and prostate cancer\",\"entity\":\"CompositeMention\",\"rationale\":\"Contiguous coordinated string naming three separate specific cancers (brain, breast, prostate) is annotated as one Composite Mention. The organism modifier 'human' is excluded.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate Section 2 - Composite Mention\"},{\"start\":295,\"end\":302,\"text\":\"cancers\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"The generic plural 'cancers' refers to a family of multiple specific diseases rather than one defined disease, so it is a Disease Class. 'human' is an organism modifier and is excluded.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate Section 1 - Disease Class\"},{\"start\":385,\"end\":397,\"text\":\"glioblastoma\",\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"The disease name 'glioblastoma' premodifies the non-molecular head noun 'cell lines', so it is a Modifier under the ordinary Modifier rule.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate Section 3 - Modifier\"},{\"start\":445,\"end\":460,\"text\":\"prostate cancer\",\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"The disease name 'prostate cancer' premodifies the non-molecular head noun 'cell lines', so it is a Modifier.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate Section 3 - Modifier\"},{\"start\":492,\"end\":505,\"text\":\"breast cancer\",\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"The disease name 'breast cancer' premodifies the non-molecular head noun 'cell lines', so it is a Modifier.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate Section 3 - Modifier\"},{\"start\":557,\"end\":578,\"text\":\"primary glioblastomas\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"The plural 'glioblastomas' with the qualifier 'primary' denotes